  "report": "# F002 weak-supervision: COMPLETED\n\nSeeds: 17, 29, 43, 71, 101. Every seed must hold every coverage and falsifier rule.\n\n- seed 17: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 29: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 43: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 71: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 101: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n\n- mutation checks of the harness (required for COMPLETED): 29 of 29 killed at de62f1bde7475fe7d114646272dc8dfd4276e555\n- mutations_ok: True\n\nLimitations: gold is the known truth of a synthetic world (GoldSource::Oracle) and the labelling functions are seeded stand-ins with known confusion matrices; nothing here is a claim about real annotators, LLM labellers or real verifiers; the majority-vote baseline carries the naive posterior (n_c + 1) / (n + C), which is far from calibrated by itself: the world with homogeneous accuracies and no verifier (w3, a descriptive control) shows a Brier and ECE gain of the same size as the one in w1, so the calibration gate supports only 'better calibrated than the naive vote-share posterior', not that Dawid-Skene or verifier precedence produces the gain; the descriptive calibrated vote shares (mvc, mvcp: true priors and a sharpening exponent fitted on pilot seeds) tie with the label model in w3 and beat it in w1 when they respect the vetoes (mvcp), which is a recorded negative result about the label model and gates nothing; the label model is not more accurate than a veto-aware majority vote in these worlds (descriptive: w1_census_accuracy_ds_permille against w1_census_accuracy_mvp_permille); the accuracy rule (census of w1) compares it with the plain majority vote only, which ignores the verifiers; verifier precedence is only as good as the verifiers: in the contaminated world (w2, 8% of the votes of a firing verifier rule out the true class) the label model is less accurate than the majority vote and an item the verifiers rule out entirely is Disputed; w2 is used for the hard veto check and the Disputed rate, and its accuracy and calibration gains are descriptive and not gated; a disputed item has no distribution, so every arm's scorer is given the uniform distribution over the classes for it; the veto check exempts exactly that substitute; the argmax of a distribution is its last maximal class and equal-mass calibration bins cut a stable sort of the confidences, so ties in confidence fall in the gold order; the majority vote carries a 1e-9 per-class-rank epsilon so that its ties go to the lowest class, which is generous to the baseline; the independent oracle is a second implementation of the same documented algorithm: it shows the product implements Dawid-Skene, resolution and the metrics as documented, not that the documentation is the only sound choice; correlated labelling functions are in the worlds (one pair) and make the posteriors overconfident, which the calibration rule measures and does not correct; the gain rules gate on the lower end of a paired bootstrap interval over the gold items; the world itself is regenerated per seed, so a seed is one world, and five seeds are five worlds, not a population statement; the mutation checker's evidence (results/mutations.json) is about the harness, not the label model; COMPLETED requires it (every planned mutation killed) as a precondition of trusting a pass, so without it the verdict is INVALID, and it says nothing about the label model itself; a panic of the product is a falsification (product_panics), contained by the harness; a panic in harness code itself is a harness fault (INVALID); timings come from one shared cloud container; no capacity claim.\n"
